# GitHub CODEOWNERS Example Configuration
#
# Lines starting with '#' are comments.
# Each line defines a file pattern followed by one or more owners (GitHub usernames or @org/teams).
# Order matters: the last matching pattern takes precedence for the specified file.
#
# To activate this configuration, copy or rename this file to:
#   .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# Documentation:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repository
* @octocat

# Security policy and critical credentials audit
/SECURITY.md @security-team
/.github/workflows/ @devops-team @octocat

# Documentation and standards
/docs/ @docs-team @octocat
/README.md @docs-team @octocat
/CONTRIBUTING.md @docs-team @octocat

# Automation and maintenance scripts
/scripts/ @devops-team

# Core application / stack-specific code (customize for your repository)
#/src/ @frontend-team
#/backend/ @backend-team
